:[{"type":"text","value":"Export adapter-specific metadata that lets hydration/persistence resume sync.\nThe payload shape is owned by the adapter."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unknown"}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getsyncmetadata","children":[{"type":"text","value":"getSyncMetadata()?"}]},{"type":"code","value":"optional getSyncMetadata: () => Record<string, unknown>;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/types.ts#L454","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/db/src/types.ts:454"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Get the sync metadata for insert operations"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"returns-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Record"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unknown"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Record containing relation information"}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"importsyncmeta","children":[{"type":"text","value":"importSyncMeta()?"}]},{"type":"code","value":"optional importSyncMeta: (meta) => void;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/types.ts#L465","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/db/src/types.ts:465"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Import adapter-specific metadata produced by exportSyncMeta."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":5,"id":"meta","children":[{"type":"text","value":"meta"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unknown"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"returns-3","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"void"}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"mergesyncmeta","children":[{"type":"text","value":"mergeSyncMeta()?"}]},{"type":"code","value":"optional mergeSyncMeta: (current, incoming) => unknown;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/types.ts#L470","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/db/src/types.ts:470"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Merge two adapter-specific metadata payloads during hydration."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"parameters-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":5,"id":"current","children":[{"type":"text","value":"current"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unknown"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":5,"id":"incoming","children":[{"type":"text","value":"incoming"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unknown"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"returns-4","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unknown"}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"rowupdatemode","children":[{"type":"text","value":"rowUpdateMode?"}]},{"type":"code","value":"optional rowUpdateMode: \"full\" | \"partial\";","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/types.ts#L479","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/db/src/types.ts:479"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The row update mode used to sync to the collection."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"default","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"partial"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"description","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"partial"},{"type":"text","value":": Updates contain only the changes to the row."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"full"},{"type":"text","value":": Updates contain the entire row."}]}]}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"sync","children":[{"type":"text","value":"sync()"}]},{"type":"code","value":"sync: (params) => \n  | void\n  | CleanupFn\n  | SyncConfigRes;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/types.ts#L423","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/db/src/types.ts:423"}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"parameters-3","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":5,"id":"params","children":[{"type":"text","value":"params"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":6,"id":"begin","children":[{"type":"text","value":"begin"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"() => "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"void"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Begin a new sync transaction."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":6,"id":"collection","children":[{"type":"text","value":"collection"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"Collection.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Collection"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"T"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TKey"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"any"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"any"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"any"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":6,"id":"commit","children":[{"type":"text","value":"commit"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"signal?"},{"type":"text","value":") => "},{"type":"link","href":"../type-aliases/SyncAppliedReceipt.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SyncAppliedReceipt"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Commit the active sync transaction in FIFO order. Core accepts it at\nonce, and an accepted transaction always applies. Returns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" when\nits writes are visible, or a receipt that resolves when they become\nvisible. While an optimistic transaction is persisting, it becomes\nvisible when that transaction settles, together with the drop of its\noptimistic state. A signal that is already aborted abandons the\ntransaction before acceptance, and the receipt rejects with an error\nnamed "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AbortError"},{"type":"text","value":". Aborting after acceptance has no effect."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":6,"id":"markerror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"markError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"error?"},{"type":"text","value":") => "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"void"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Signal that initial sync failed before producing a usable snapshot.\nWhen supplied, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"error"},{"type":"text","value":" is preserved as the rejection reason from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"preload()"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":6,"id":"markready","children":[{"type":"text","value":"markReady"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"() => "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"void"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Signal that a usable initial or recovered snapshot is available."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":6,"id":"metadata","children":[{"type":"text","value":"metadata?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"SyncMetadataApi.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SyncMetadataApi"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TKey"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":6,"id":"truncate","children":[{"type":"text","value":"truncate"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"truncate({ markReady: false })"},{"type":"text","value":" replaces synced rows without changing Collection\nstatus. Omitting the option preserves the default behavior of marking the\nCollection ready. The last truncate in one transaction supplies its readiness\nintent; the last replacement in one published batch supplies that batch's intent."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"(options?: { markReady?: boolean }) => "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"void"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":6,"id":"write","children":[{"type":"text","value":"write"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"message"},{"type":"text","value":") => "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"void"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"returns-5","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"| "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"void"},{"type":"text","value":"\n| "},{"type":"link","href":"../type-aliases/CleanupFn.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CleanupFn"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n| "},{"type":"link","href":"../type-aliases/SyncConfigRes.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SyncConfigRes"}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"t","text":"T","level":3},{"id":"tkey","text":"TKey","level":3},{"id":"properties","text":"Properties","level":2},{"id":"exportsyncmeta","text":"exportSyncMeta()?","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":4},{"id":"getsyncmetadata","text":"getSyncMetadata()?","level":3},{"id":"returns-2","text":"Returns","level":4},{"id":"importsyncmeta","text":"importSyncMeta()?","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":4},{"id":"meta","text":"meta","level":5},{"id":"returns-3","text":"Returns","level":4},{"id":"mergesyncmeta","text":"mergeSyncMeta()?","level":3},{"id":"parameters-2","text":"Parameters","level":4},{"id":"current","text":"current","level":5},{"id":"incoming","text":"incoming","level":5},{"id":"returns-4","text":"Returns","level":4},{"id":"rowupdatemode","text":"rowUpdateMode?","level":3},{"id":"default","text":"Default","level":4},{"id":"description","text":"Description","level":4},{"id":"sync","text":"sync()","level":3},{"id":"parameters-3","text":"Parameters","level":4},{"id":"params","text":"params","level":5},{"id":"begin","text":"begin","level":6},{"id":"collection","text":"collection","level":6},{"id":"commit","text":"commit","level":6},{"id":"markerror","text":"markError","level":6},{"id":"markready","text":"markReady","level":6},{"id":"metadata","text":"metadata?","level":6},{"id":"truncate","text":"truncate","level":6},{"id":"write","text":"write","level":6},{"id":"returns-5","text":"Returns","level":4}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nDefined in: [packages/db/src/types.ts:419](https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/types.ts#L419)\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### T\n\n`T` *extends* `object` = `Record`\\<`string`, `unknown`\\>\n\n### TKey\n\n`TKey` *extends* `string` \\| `number` = `string` \\| `number`\n\n## Properties\n\n### exportSyncMeta()?\n\n```ts\noptional exportSyncMeta: () => unknown;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/db/src/types.ts:460](https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/types.ts#L460)\n\nExport adapter-specific metadata that lets hydration/persistence resume sync.\nThe payload shape is owned by the adapter.\n\n#### Returns\n\n`unknown`\n\n***\n\n### getSyncMetadata()?\n\n```ts\noptional getSyncMetadata: () => Record<string, unknown>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/db/src/types.ts:454](https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/types.ts#L454)\n\nGet the sync metadata for insert operations\n\n#### Returns\n\n`Record`\\<`string`, `unknown`\\>\n\nRecord containing relation information\n\n***\n\n### importSyncMeta()?\n\n```ts\noptional importSyncMeta: (meta) => void;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/db/src/types.ts:465](https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/types.ts#L465)\n\nImport adapter-specific metadata produced by exportSyncMeta.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### meta\n\n`unknown`\n\n#### Returns\n\n`void`\n\n***\n\n### mergeSyncMeta()?\n\n```ts\noptional mergeSyncMeta: (current, incoming) => unknown;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/db/src/types.ts:470](https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/types.ts#L470)\n\nMerge two adapter-specific metadata payloads during hydration.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### current\n\n`unknown`\n\n##### incoming\n\n`unknown`\n\n#### Returns\n\n`unknown`\n\n***\n\n### rowUpdateMode?\n\n```ts\noptional rowUpdateMode: \"full\" | \"partial\";\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/db/src/types.ts:479](https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/types.ts#L479)\n\nThe row update mode used to sync to the collection.\n\n#### Default\n\n`partial`\n\n#### Description\n\n- `partial`: Updates contain only the changes to the row.\n- `full`: Updates contain the entire row.\n\n***\n\n### sync()\n\n```ts\nsync: (params) => \n  | void\n  | CleanupFn\n  | SyncConfigRes;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/db/src/types.ts:423](https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/types.ts#L423)\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### params\n\n###### begin\n\n() => `void`\n\nBegin a new sync transaction.\n\n###### collection\n\n[`Collection`](Collection.md)\\<`T`, `TKey`, `any`, `any`, `any`\\>\n\n###### commit\n\n(`signal?`) => [`SyncAppliedReceipt`](../type-aliases/SyncAppliedReceipt.md)\n\nCommit the active sync transaction in FIFO order. Core accepts it at\nonce, and an accepted transaction always applies. Returns `true` when\nits writes are visible, or a receipt that resolves when they become\nvisible. While an optimistic transaction is persisting, it becomes\nvisible when that transaction settles, together with the drop of its\noptimistic state. A signal that is already aborted abandons the\ntransaction before acceptance, and the receipt rejects with an error\nnamed `AbortError`. Aborting after acceptance has no effect.\n\n###### markError\n\n(`error?`) => `void`\n\nSignal that initial sync failed before producing a usable snapshot.\nWhen supplied, `error` is preserved as the rejection reason from `preload()`.\n\n###### markReady\n\n() => `void`\n\nSignal that a usable initial or recovered snapshot is available.\n\n###### metadata?\n\n[`SyncMetadataApi`](SyncMetadataApi.md)\\<`TKey`\\>\n\n###### truncate\n\n`truncate({ markReady: false })` replaces synced rows without changing Collection\nstatus. Omitting the option preserves the default behavior of marking the\nCollection ready. The last truncate in one transaction supplies its readiness\nintent; the last replacement in one published batch supplies that batch's intent.\n\n(options?: { markReady?: boolean }) => `void`\n\n###### write\n\n(`message`) => `void`\n\n#### Returns\n\n  \\| `void`\n  \\| [`CleanupFn`](../type-aliases/CleanupFn.md)\n  \\| [`SyncConfigRes`](../type-aliases/SyncConfigRes.md)\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: SyncConfig\ntitle: SyncConfig\n---\n\nDefined in: [packages/db/src/types.ts:419](https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/types.ts#L419)\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### T\n\n`T` *extends* `object` = `Record`\\<`string`, `unknown`\\>\n\n### TKey\n\n`TKey` *extends* `string` \\| `number` = `string` \\| `number`\n\n## Properties\n\n### exportSyncMeta()?\n\n```ts\noptional exportSyncMeta: () => unknown;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/db/src/types.ts:460](https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/types.ts#L460)\n\nExport adapter-specific metadata that lets hydration/persistence resume sync.\nThe payload shape is owned by the adapter.\n\n#### Returns\n\n`unknown`\n\n***\n\n### getSyncMetadata()?\n\n```ts\noptional getSyncMetadata: () => Record<string, unknown>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/db/src/types.ts:454](https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/types.ts#L454)\n\nGet the sync metadata for insert operations\n\n#### Returns\n\n`Record`\\<`string`, `unknown`\\>\n\nRecord containing relation information\n\n***\n\n### importSyncMeta()?\n\n```ts\noptional importSyncMeta: (meta) => void;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/db/src/types.ts:465](https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/types.ts#L465)\n\nImport adapter-specific metadata produced by exportSyncMeta.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### meta\n\n`unknown`\n\n#### Returns\n\n`void`\n\n***\n\n### mergeSyncMeta()?\n\n```ts\noptional mergeSyncMeta: (current, incoming) => unknown;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/db/src/types.ts:470](https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/types.ts#L470)\n\nMerge two adapter-specific metadata payloads during hydration.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### current\n\n`unknown`\n\n##### incoming\n\n`unknown`\n\n#### Returns\n\n`unknown`\n\n***\n\n### rowUpdateMode?\n\n```ts\noptional rowUpdateMode: \"full\" | \"partial\";\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/db/src/types.ts:479](https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/types.ts#L479)\n\nThe row update mode used to sync to the collection.\n\n#### Default\n\n`partial`\n\n#### Description\n\n- `partial`: Updates contain only the changes to the row.\n- `full`: Updates contain the entire row.\n\n***\n\n### sync()\n\n```ts\nsync: (params) => \n  | void\n  | CleanupFn\n  | SyncConfigRes;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/db/src/types.ts:423](https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/types.ts#L423)\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### params\n\n###### begin\n\n() => `void`\n\nBegin a new sync transaction.\n\n###### collection\n\n[`Collection`](Collection.md)\\<`T`, `TKey`, `any`, `any`, `any`\\>\n\n###### commit\n\n(`signal?`) => [`SyncAppliedReceipt`](../type-aliases/SyncAppliedReceipt.md)\n\nCommit the active sync transaction in FIFO order. Core accepts it at\nonce, and an accepted transaction always applies. Returns `true` when\nits writes are visible, or a receipt that resolves when they become\nvisible. While an optimistic transaction is persisting, it becomes\nvisible when that transaction settles, together with the drop of its\noptimistic state. A signal that is already aborted abandons the\ntransaction before acceptance, and the receipt rejects with an error\nnamed `AbortError`. Aborting after acceptance has no effect.\n\n###### markError\n\n(`error?`) => `void`\n\nSignal that initial sync failed before producing a usable snapshot.\nWhen supplied, `error` is preserved as the rejection reason from `preload()`.\n\n###### markReady\n\n() => `void`\n\nSignal that a usable initial or recovered snapshot is available.\n\n###### metadata?\n\n[`SyncMetadataApi`](SyncMetadataApi.md)\\<`TKey`\\>\n\n###### truncate\n\n`truncate({ markReady: false })` replaces synced rows without changing Collection\nstatus. Omitting the option preserves the default behavior of marking the\nCollection ready. The last truncate in one transaction supplies its readiness\nintent; the last replacement in one published batch supplies that batch's intent.\n\n(options?: { markReady?: boolean }) => `void`\n\n###### write\n\n(`message`) => `void`\n\n#### Returns\n\n  \\| `void`\n  \\| [`CleanupFn`](../type-aliases/CleanupFn.md)\n  \\| [`SyncConfigRes`](../type-aliases/SyncConfigRes.md)\n"}
